content.text:
Note: The pushed rail objects now no longer have group — unused. Good.

There is a potential bug in `buildRail` post calls: `quat.identity()` mutates quat, but then for each subsequent post, quat is already identity. Fine. But note: after the loop, `quat` stays identity. bands create their own. Fine.

Palms: original trunk created geometry per segment then group scaled. Our matrix scale: radius ratio * scale, y 1.25*scale. But original CylinderGeometry height 1.25 centered; position y 0.6+i*1.18 then scaled by group scale. Our position (0.6+i*1.18)*scale and geometry scale y 1.25*scale. Correct.

But trunk geometry radius base .2 vs original radii .18-.22 taper; minor.

Leaves: original geometry shape fixed; group scaled. Position (px,9.6,pz) scaled. Our pos multiplied and scale. Good.

Now contact shadow in skater.js. Add constructor setup after body build. Need texture canvas. Let's add method `_buildContactShadow`. In update, use s.groundY. Also in reset position.

Implementation:

```js
_buildContactShadow() {
  const c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width=c.height=128;
  const ctx = c.getContext('2d');
  const grad = ctx.createRadialGradient(64,64,4,64,64,62);
  grad.addColorStop(0,'rgba(0,0,0,0.62)');
  grad.addColorStop(0.55,'rgba(0,0,0,0.34)');
  grad.addColorStop(1,'rgba(0,0,0,0)');
  ctx.fillStyle=grad; ctx.fillRect(0,0,128,128);
  const tex = new THREE.CanvasTexture(c);
  tex.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;
  const mat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({map:tex, transparent:true, depthWrite:false, opacity:0.75, toneMapped:false});
  const geo = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(2.1, 3.0);
  geo.rotateX(-Math.PI/2); // plane in XZ, length along z
  this.contactShadow = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat);
  this.contactShadow.renderOrder = 2;
  this.contactShadow.visible = false;
  this.scene.add(this.contactShadow);
}
```

Plane rotation X -PI/2 maps original XY to XZ: local y -> -z, so width x, length z. Good.

Update:
```js
const gy = s.groundY;
if (Number.isFinite(gy)) {
  const height = Math.max(0, s.y - gy);
  const fade = Math.max(0, 1 - height / 4.5);
  this.contactShadow.visible = fade > 0.02 && (s.bail||0) >= 0;
  this.contactShadow.position.set(s.x, gy + 0.018, s.z);
  this.contactShadow.rotation.y = s.heading;
  const sc = 1 + height*0.18;
  this.contactShadow.scale.set(sc, 1, sc);
  mat.opacity = 0.62*fade*fade...
}
```
Material accessible this.contactShadow.material. Note plane geometry rotated; rotating mesh around Y after geometry rotation is fine.

Also hide when group invisible? In update group visibility set elsewhere via show(). Contact shadow in menu: skater group is visible? In menu, `show()` maybe called. Actually menu skater visible after `show()`? Let's check main. The contact shadow visible based on groundY, which we'll pass in menu. Fine.

Potential double shadow with sun but it's subtle.

Add call in constructor before traverse (traverse only group so shadow unaffected).

Now pass groundY in main. We need heightAt imported already at top (yes). In visual object playing add groundY. In paused/menu/results add too.

